# TACET rules (short version; full docs in /docs)

Read `docs/MEMORY.md` and `docs/RULES.md` before starting any task.

## Never
- Print, log, commit or paste secrets or `.env*` contents. Use env var NAMES only.
- Rename the MongoDB DB (`seeby`), collections, Neo4j labels, connection strings, or the `syncin.vercel.app` URL.
- Run scripts that write to a database without asking. Read any script before running it.
- Trust client-supplied identity or role. Every API route authenticates and scopes by role and ownership.
- Return answer keys to students (`referenceSolution`, `expectedResult`, `referenceQuery`, hidden test cases stay `select:false`).
- Add hardcoded secret fallbacks. Throw if a required env var is missing.
- Commit `public/fonts/melodrame.*`, `uploads/`, `.env*`, `node_modules`, `.next`, scratch files.
- Introduce the names SEBBY, SEEBY, SyncIn or Rhiley in new code or copy.

## Always
- Brand: `TACET` in wordmarks/headings, `Tacet` in sentences. Agents are Seashell, Shellfish, Sand Flea.
- Use `AUTH_COOKIE_NAME` / `AUTH_STORAGE_KEY` from `lib/constants/auth.ts`. Parse profile IDs with `/^(syncin|tacet)@/`.
- Fonts: `font-display` (Melodrame) only for wordmark + landing hero; `font-serif` headings; `font-sans` body; `font-mono` data.
- Tailwind v4: define tokens in `@theme` in `globals.css`. Don't rely on `tailwind.config.js`.
- One concern per commit. Check `git diff --stat` before committing.
- Run `npm run build` and typecheck, then verify in a real browser or with real API calls. Show evidence; never claim "verified" without it.
- On Windows PowerShell, write a script file instead of long inline `node -e`.
- Append durable learnings to `docs/MEMORY.md`; log decisions in `docs/DECISIONS.md`; update `docs/TASKS.md`.
- Stop and wait when told to stop.
